## Design decisions

- **Item count**: ICU plural in the ARB file. Arabic gets all six CLDR categories (`zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other`). Vietnamese has no grammatical plural, so it only needs `other`, plus an optional `=0` empty state.
- **Total price**: format the amount in Dart with `NumberFormat.simpleCurrency(locale:, name:)` and pass it as a placeholder into a complete sentence. ARB `optionalParameters` are fixed at build time, so they can't take a runtime currency code.
- **Currency comes from your cart data, not the locale.** An Arabic UI showing a USD cart should still show USD. Never derive the currency or language from the country.
- **Fallback**: match on language code, otherwise use English. No locale override is saved unless the user picks one.

