Here's how to add a protected `/orders/:orderId` deep link to an existing go_router setup. It covers routing, the auth guard with a safe return path, the order screen, platform link config, and tests. Adapt names (`AuthController`, `OrderRepository`, etc.) to what your app already has.

## 1. Route definition

Nest the details route under the orders list. A cold-start deep link then still gets a sensible back stack (`/orders` → `/orders/123`).

```dart
// lib/router/app_router.dart
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';
import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';

GoRouter createRouter(AuthController auth) {
  return GoRouter(
    initialLocation: '/',
    refreshListenable: auth, // re-runs redirect on login/logout
    redirect: (context, state) => _authRedirect(auth, state),
    routes: [
      GoRoute(path: '/', builder: (_, __) => const HomeScreen()),
      GoRoute(path: '/splash', builder: (_, __) => const SplashScreen()),
      GoRoute(
        path: '/login',
        builder: (_, state) => LoginScreen(
          from: state.uri.queryParameters['from'],
        ),
      ),
      GoRoute(
        path: '/orders',
        builder: (_, __) => const OrdersScreen(),
        routes: [
          GoRoute(
            path: ':orderId',
            name: 'orderDetails',
            redirect: (_, state) {
              final id = state.pathParameters['orderId']!;
              return _isValidOrderId(id) ? null : '/orders';
            },
            builder: (_, state) => OrderDetailsScreen(
              orderId: state.pathParameters['orderId']!,
            ),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    ],
  );
}

final _orderIdPattern = RegExp(r'^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$');
bool _isValidOrderId(String id) => _orderIdPattern.hasMatch(id);
```

## 2. Auth guard that preserves the deep link

```dart
const _publicPaths = {'/', '/login', '/splash'};

String? _authRedirect(AuthController auth, GoRouterState state) {
  final path = state.uri.path;

  // Auth state still restoring (e.g. reading a token on cold start):
  // park on splash so we don't bounce a valid user to login.
  if (auth.status == AuthStatus.unknown) {
    return path == '/splash' ? null : '/splash';
  }

  final loggedIn = auth.status == AuthStatus.authenticated;
  final isPublic = _publicPaths.contains(path);

  if (!loggedIn && !isPublic) {
    final from = Uri.encodeComponent(state.uri.toString());
    return '/login?from=$from';
  }

  if (loggedIn && (path == '/login' || path == '/splash')) {
    return safeReturnPath(state.uri.queryParameters['from']) ?? '/';
  }

  return null;
}

/// Only allow internal, relative paths. This prevents open redirects
/// like ?from=https://evil.example or ?from=//evil.example.
String? safeReturnPath(String? raw) {
  if (raw == null || raw.isEmpty) return null;
  final uri = Uri.tryParse(raw);
  if (uri == null || uri.hasScheme || uri.hasAuthority) return null;
  if (!uri.path.startsWith('/') || uri.path.startsWith('//')) return null;
  return uri.toString();
}
```

Note that `/splash` loses the `from` param in this simple version. If cold-start restore is slow, carry it the same way: `'/splash?from=...'`.

`AuthController` should be a `ChangeNotifier` (or wrap your stream/Riverpod/Bloc state in one) exposing `status`, and call `notifyListeners()` when it changes:

```dart
enum AuthStatus { unknown, authenticated, unauthenticated }

class AuthController extends ChangeNotifier {
  AuthStatus _status = AuthStatus.unknown;
  AuthStatus get status => _status;

  void setStatus(AuthStatus s) {
    if (s == _status) return;
    _status = s;
    notifyListeners();
  }
}
```

After a successful login, either let `refreshListenable` trigger the redirect above, or navigate explicitly:

```dart
context.go(safeReturnPath(widget.from) ?? '/');
```

## 3. Order details screen: authorization, not just authentication

Being logged in doesn't mean the user owns order `123`. The backend must enforce ownership. The screen should handle 403 and 404 the same way so it doesn't reveal whether an order exists.

```dart
class OrderDetailsScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const OrderDetailsScreen({super.key, required this.orderId});
  final String orderId;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Order details')),
      body: FutureBuilder<Order>(
        future: context.read<OrderRepository>().fetchOrder(orderId),
        builder: (context, snap) {
          if (snap.connectionState != ConnectionState.done) {
            return const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator());
          }
          final err = snap.error;
          if (err is OrderNotFound || err is OrderForbidden) {
            return const _Message('Order not found.');
          }
          if (err is Unauthorized) {
            // Session expired server-side.
            WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback(
              (_) => context.read<AuthController>()
                  .setStatus(AuthStatus.unauthenticated),
            );
            return const SizedBox.shrink();
          }
          if (err != null) return const _Message('Could not load order.');
          return OrderView(order: snap.data!);
        },
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

In real code, cache the future in a `StatefulWidget` or your state manager so it doesn't refetch on every rebuild.

Navigate in-app with:

```dart
context.goNamed('orderDetails', pathParameters: {'orderId': order.id});
```

## 4. Platform deep link configuration

Prefer verified HTTPS links (App Links / Universal Links) over a custom scheme, since other apps can't claim them.

**Android** (`android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`, inside the main `<activity>`):

```xml
<intent-filter android:autoVerify="true">
    <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
    <data android:scheme="https"
          android:host="example.com"
          android:pathPrefix="/orders" />
</intent-filter>
```

Host `https://example.com/.well-known/assetlinks.json` with your package name and SHA-256 signing cert fingerprints. Include the Play App Signing key as well as your upload/debug keys.

**iOS:**
- In Xcode → Runner → Signing & Capabilities → Associated Domains, add `applinks:example.com`.
- Host `https://example.com/.well-known/apple-app-site-association` (no extension, `application/json`):

```json
{
  "applinks": {
    "details": [{
      "appIDs": ["TEAMID.com.example.app"],
      "components": [{ "/": "/orders/*" }]
    }]
  }
}
```

On recent Flutter versions, Flutter deep linking is on by default. If your `Info.plist` or manifest sets `FlutterDeepLinkingEnabled` / `flutter_deeplinking_enabled` to `false` (common if you previously used `app_links`/`uni_links`), remove it or set it to `true`. Don't run two deep link handlers at once.

## 5. Tests

**Router/guard widget tests:**

```dart
testWidgets('logged-out deep link goes to login and preserves target',
    (tester) async {
  final auth = AuthController()..setStatus(AuthStatus.unauthenticated);
  final router = createRouter(auth)..go('/orders/abc123');
  await tester.pumpWidget(_app(router, auth));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();

  expect(router.state.uri.path, '/login');
  expect(router.state.uri.queryParameters['from'], '/orders/abc123');

  auth.setStatus(AuthStatus.authenticated);
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();
  expect(router.state.uri.path, '/orders/abc123');
});

testWidgets('invalid order id falls back to list', (tester) async {
  final auth = AuthController()..setStatus(AuthStatus.authenticated);
  final router = createRouter(auth)..go('/orders/%3Cscript%3E');
  await tester.pumpWidget(_app(router, auth));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();
  expect(router.state.uri.path, '/orders');
});

test('safeReturnPath rejects external targets', () {
  expect(safeReturnPath('https://evil.example'), isNull);
  expect(safeReturnPath('//evil.example'), isNull);
  expect(safeReturnPath('/orders/1'), '/orders/1');
});
```

(`router.state` requires go_router ≥ 14. On older versions, use `router.routerDelegate.currentConfiguration.uri`.)

**Manual device checks:**

```sh
# Android
adb shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW \
  -d "https://example.com/orders/abc123" com.example.app
adb shell pm get-app-links com.example.app   # verify domain status

# iOS simulator
xcrun simctl openurl booted "https://example.com/orders/abc123"
```

Test all four combinations: cold start vs. app in background, and logged in vs. logged out.

## Checklist
- [ ] `/orders/:orderId` nested under `/orders` for a correct back stack
- [ ] Global redirect sends unauthenticated users to `/login?from=<encoded>`
- [ ] `from` validated as an internal path (no open redirect)
- [ ] Unknown-auth state handled (splash) so cold-start links aren't lost
- [ ] `refreshListenable` wired to auth changes
- [ ] Order ID format validated; 403/404 shown as "not found"
- [ ] Server enforces order ownership
- [ ] assetlinks.json and AASA hosted; manifest and entitlements updated
- [ ] Widget tests plus device tests for cold and warm starts

