## Review: `softWrap: false` does not make a title single-line

The teammate's assumption is backwards. `softWrap` and `maxLines` control different things, and neither overrides the other:

| Property | Controls | Effect of `\n` in the text |
|---|---|---|
| `softWrap: false` | Whether text **wraps automatically** at the width limit. | None. Hard line breaks still start new lines. |
| `maxLines: 1` | The total number of laid-out lines, whether from wrapping or from `\n`. | Lines after the first are cut off. |

With `softWrap: false` and no `maxLines`, server copy like `"Weekend\nSale"` renders as **two lines**. The compact layout grows taller or overflows its parent. Width overflow is also not handled, because the line just runs past the edge and gets clipped.

### Recommended fix

Set the constraint explicitly, and normalize the copy so the user doesn't silently lose the text after the first newline:

```dart
String singleLine(String s) =>
    s.replaceAll(RegExp(r'[\r\n\u2028\u2029]+'), ' ').trim();

Text(
  singleLine(title),
  maxLines: 1,
  softWrap: false,              // optional once maxLines: 1 is set
  overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,
)
```

Why each part matters:
- **`maxLines: 1`** is the actual guarantee of one line. Keep it even after sanitizing, since it protects against any unnormalized input.
- **Sanitizing** turns `"Weekend\nSale"` into `"Weekend Sale…"`. Without it you would get `"Weekend…"` and lose "Sale" entirely. It also covers `\r\n` and the Unicode line/paragraph separators.
- **`overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis`** handles long single-line copy cleanly. Without it the text is clipped mid-glyph.

If the design team prefers to show only the first line, skip the sanitizing. Keep `maxLines: 1` either way.

### Regression check

Put the title in its own widget (e.g. `CompactTitle`). Then test that it lays out as exactly one line, both for newline copy and for long copy at a larger text scale:

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter/rendering.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

Future<RenderParagraph> pumpTitle(
  WidgetTester tester,
  String text, {
  double width = 160,
  double textScale = 1.0,
}) async {
  await tester.pumpWidget(
    MaterialApp(
      home: MediaQuery(
        data: MediaQueryData(textScaler: TextScaler.linear(textScale)),
        child: Center(
          child: SizedBox(width: width, child: CompactTitle(title: text)),
        ),
      ),
    ),
  );
  return tester.renderObject<RenderParagraph>(
    find.descendant(of: find.byType(CompactTitle), matching: find.byType(RichText)),
  );
}

void main() {
  const cases = {
    'LF': 'Weekend\nSale',
    'CRLF': 'Weekend\r\nSale',
    'multiple breaks': 'A\n\nB\nC',
    'unicode separator': 'Weekend\u2028Sale',
    'long single line': 'An extremely long promotional title that cannot fit',
  };

  for (final scale in [1.0, 2.0]) {
    cases.forEach((name, text) {
      testWidgets('CompactTitle is one line: $name @${scale}x', (tester) async {
        final reference = await pumpTitle(tester, 'A', textScale: scale);
        final oneLineHeight = reference.size.height;

        final paragraph = await pumpTitle(tester, text, textScale: scale);

        expect(paragraph.size.height, oneLineHeight,
            reason: 'title must render as exactly one line');
        expect(paragraph.text.toPlainText(), isNot(contains('\n')));
        expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
      });
    });
  }
}
```

How this catches the bug:
- **The height comparison** against a one-character reference is the core assertion. It fails right away if someone removes `maxLines` again, because `"Weekend\nSale"` lays out two lines tall.
- **The "no newline in rendered text" check** pins the sanitizing behavior, so content after a break stays visible.
- **The long-copy and 2× scale cases** cover truncation instead of overflow.
- **Optionally**, add a golden test of the newline case at the compact width so the ellipsis placement is locked in visually.

